+- **UX-16 — Private quizzes:** A SchoolQuiz account enters a flat HARD quiz for one sitting, without deferred resume. New creation defaults are `maxAttempts=1`, `show-result=false`, no link expiry; saved settings remain intact. Authors may choose a limit ≥1, result visibility and an expiry or no end date, and disable the link earlier. Each new start atomically requires enabled access, server time before optional expiry and `startedCount < currentLimit`. Changing the limit preserves the count; increasing it permits only the remaining difference. Link closure or lowering the limit does not end an authorized active attempt or extend its original AD-31 deadlines. Retry returns the original operation. Current show-result applies to all own results, including past read/retry: false gives only completion, true permits own N/M and percent; author statistics remain. Server redaction and newer-setting/cache fencing prevent hidden-data recovery; visibility does not recalculate scores or reset attempts. STANDARD/PLASMA entry, hints and paid-correct skips are unavailable; no replacement fee is inferred. Recovery timeout preserves timely answers and counts all remaining/unissued questions unanswered over the entire frozen quiz using ordinary HARD arithmetic, retaining the timeout reason and current visibility. Sources: EXPERIENCE F11/O4, DESIGN private controls, AD-29/31; CAP-25. O4 product choices are closed; the named server adapters remain work. No new pass/fail, refund, re-enable, renewal or rotation requirement is introduced.
 
-## Still requiring confirmation
+- **UX-17 — Review and translation:** TESTING records one independent 1–3 rating per question/revision against the captured server threshold, default 2; there is no averaging/quorum gate. Other required directions remain. Validation confirms or returns the question/stage and advances after authoritative ACK; return identifies the failed stage without a reason field. Private quizzes do not enter public return-for-revision. Translation changes the actual source/target pair and restores that pair's draft/position. Segment review is unchecked/correct/error; selecting the same decision clears it, missing translation cannot be correct, and required segment decisions gate next/final submission. Online save recovery does not pause an active question clock. A completed review cycle includes justified rejection for payment; curator removal of published content has its separate reason rule. Sources: EXPERIENCE F9, AD-26 and retained review/economy contracts.
 
